# Table columns: badge, tag, or plain text

**Language:** English. User rule, 2026-11-09. Applies to every module (Admin, Content, BOM, SPEC, Part Search, Unified Search, Release Notes), in Figma and in code.

**One idea:** a "Type" column is the one place where different values get different colours (plus file types). Everything else is a badge, a tone tag, a neutral tag or plain text.

## Which treatment for which column

| Column kind | Treatment | Figma | Examples |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Status of a record, or access state | Dot + label, left aligned | `Badge__Status`, table cell `type=badge` | Draft / Published, Active / Error, Enabled / Disabled, Allowed / Not allowed, Ready / Needs review, Included / Excluded |
| Confidence or match quality | Tone tag | `Tag__Status` | High / Medium / Low, Added manually |
| Content file type | Colourful tag by fixed table | `Tag__Colorful` (see `content-file-type-tags.mdc`) | RFA, PDF, DWG |
| Small closed **Type** (every "Type" column) | Colourful tag, one fixed colour per value, border on | `Tag__Colorful` | Admin / User, System / Custom, Domain / Email, Feature / Fix / Improvement |
| Roles, labels the user creates | Neutral tag | `Tag` | Users → Roles, Knowledge Center categories |
| Everything else | Plain text | | Category, division, manufacturer, version, unit, counts, quantities, dates, Yes / No, feed format (CSV / JSON / XML) |

## Rules

- A record status is never a tag (`Tag__Status` or `Tag__Colorful`). See the status badge rule.
- A count is never a tag. Write "2 matches" as plain text.
- A value keeps one colour on every screen, in Figma and in code. Never recolour it per module.
- Colourful tags are for Type columns and file types only. Roles, categories and other labels stay neutral.
- Colours repeat across different columns (only 10 presets), but never inside one column.

## Type colours (2026-11-09)

Full lookup, including file types: `Documentation/type-tag-colors.md`. Keep both in sync.

| Column | Value | `Tag__Colorful` colour |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Users → Type | Admin | `volcano` |
| Users → Type | User | `blue` |
| Company Roles → Type, Admin Roles → System Role | System | `geekblue` |
| Company Roles → Type | Custom | `gold` |
| Access Blacklist → Type | Domain | `purple` |
| Access Blacklist → Type | Email | `cyan` |
| Release Notes → Type | Feature | `green` |
| Release Notes → Type | Improvement | `blue` |
| Release Notes → Type | Fix | `orange` |

A new Type value takes a free preset and is added to this table.
- "New" markers keep one colour everywhere the marker appears.
- Tag columns align left.

## Decisions (2026-11-09)

- Every Type column uses colourful tags, a different colour per value (see Type colours).
- Knowledge Center feed Format: plain text.
- Yes / No facts: plain text. Access and permission state (Allowed / Not allowed, Enabled / Disabled): badge.
- Admin Roles System Role: tag "System" when true, empty when not.
- Users → Roles stays neutral.
